There are at least two senses of 'government'. One is the abstraction of
'govern' ({zu'o turni}). Another is the mass of people, divided into various
institutions, which does the governing; I think this is {truci'e}. Another
(used in Britain IIRC, but not in the US) is the group composed of the PM &
his ministers (& maybe their staffs) in their executive function.

